# What graphify may read when building the code graph.
#
# graphify already honours .gitignore, which does most of the work here: it
# keeps venv/ out (15,273 of this repo's 15,473 .py files are site-packages),
# along with node_modules/, secrets and every client-data file. This file only
# handles the two places .gitignore is the WRONG filter for a code graph.
#
# Patterns here are evaluated LAST and win on conflict, so a "!" line re-includes
# something .gitignore dropped, and a plain line excludes something .gitignore
# would have allowed.

# --- Re-include: docs .gitignore drops as a side effect ----------------------
# .gitignore:139 is a blanket `*.md`, negated only for README.md, skills/** and
# deploy/**. HANDOVER.md is the architectural map of this project — the single
# most useful non-code file in the graph — and it is not tracked by git at all.
!HANDOVER.md

# --- Stay out, regardless of what .gitignore says ----------------------------
# These are listed explicitly rather than inherited. .gitignore is edited for
# git's reasons, and a future loosening there must NOT silently pull client
# data or credentials into a graph that gets queried and quoted back.

# Credentials and key material
.env
*.env.*
.app_secret_key

# Client and project data
project_data.db*
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
neo4j_backup_*.json
uploads/
projects/
models/
logs/
BI/
generated_docs/

# Vendored / generated / binary — no useful edges, large parse cost
venv/
.venv/
env/
node_modules/
__pycache__/
lib/
dist/
build/
FabricBI_beta/dist/
tools/pbi-inspector/win-x64/
.registry_cache/
*.pbix
*.pbiviz
*.exe
*.png
*.pptx
*.docx

# graphify's own output — never feed the graph back into itself
graphify-out/
